@assess_situation
title: Assess the political situation
subtitle: Where do things actually stand?
on-arrival: coup_monitoring_timer = 3; coup_exposed += 1;
go-to: 1963_main

We have spent the opening weeks of the year taking stock. The picture that emerges is not comforting, but it is clear.

Goulart is not our man — he never was — but the forces gathering around his government represent something real. The CGT general strikes, the peasant leagues, the sergeants and enlisted men who are beginning to organize: these are not Goulart's creation. They are the pressure from below that has carried him further left than he intended to go, and they will carry him further still if they are organized.

The right is also organizing. The IPES — *Instituto de Pesquisas e Estudos Sociais* — is coordinating business opposition to reform, funding media campaigns, and maintaining quiet contact with ESG officers who have already decided that Goulart must go. The CIA's presence in this is not subtle, if you know where to look.

The window is real. It is also closing.

@prepare_cadres
title: Begin preparing cadres for what is coming
subtitle: Accelerate training and security discipline across our cells.
on-arrival: clandestine_security += 2; cadre_training_timer = 4; pcdb_militia_strength += 0.3; resources -= 1;
go-to: 1963_main

We cannot afford to be caught unprepared again. The lesson of 1935 — of the *Intentona*, of Prestes in chains, of the party's decade in ruins — is too expensive to relearn. We begin the year with a systematic review of cell security, of contact protocols, of escape routes and safe houses and the identities of every cadre whose cover we are not certain of.

It is unglamorous work. The youth militants find it frustrating — they want action, not security reviews. But a cadre arrested is a cadre who talks, eventually, under enough pressure. And the DOPS applies pressure with great professional thoroughness.

@deepen_northeast
title: Intensify work in the Northeast
subtitle: Build our presence where the land question burns hottest.
on-arrival: northeast_presence += 2; rural_pcdb += 3; leagues_relation += 5; coup_progress += 1; dops_penetration += 1;
go-to: 1963_main

We send cadres north. They travel by bus through the dry interior of Pernambuco and Paraíba, through the *sertão* that the drought has turned to dust again, into the communities where Julião's leagues have already done years of work that we are only now arriving to build on.

The conditions are extraordinary. The *camponeses* are not waiting to be organized — they are already organized, already angry, already prepared to act in ways that would terrify the comfortable left in Rio. What they lack is theory, direction, connection to a broader movement. We can offer some of that.

The landlords notice. The state police notice. DOPS notices. Our visibility in the Northeast is also our exposure.

@watch_and_wait
title: Observe and consolidate
subtitle: Do not move until the situation clarifies.
on-arrival: clandestine_security += 1; resources += 1; maoist_dissent += 5; youth_dissent += 8;
go-to: 1963_main

The gradualists argue for patience. The objective conditions are still forming; the mass organizations are not yet strong enough to sustain a confrontation; the party's security is not yet robust enough to survive the repression that an early move would bring down on us. Wait. Build. Let the contradictions deepen.

The Maoist faction and the youth disagree — loudly. Every month we wait is a month the right uses to strengthen its position. But we hold the line, for now. Patience is also a discipline.

@1963_main
new-page: false

Whatever path we have chosen, the year stretches ahead: full of the particular dread of knowing that history is accelerating toward a point of rupture, and that the side which is better prepared will determine what comes after.

The coup is coming. We do not yet know when. We do not yet know if we can stop it — or survive it — or turn it into something else entirely.

But we are here. The party exists. That is not nothing.